      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we need to calculate the magnitude of their cross product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\).\n\nFirst, we compute the cross product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\). The cross product of two vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} u_1 \\\\ u_2 \\\\ u_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\\\ v_2 \\\\ v_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by the determinant of the following matrix:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4 \\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nExpanding this determinant, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{i} \\left(1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)\\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left(3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1\\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left(3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1\\right)\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the expressions inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{i} (4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j} (12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k} (-9 - 1) = \\mathbf{i} (-2) - \\mathbf{j} (14) + \\mathbf{k} (-10) = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of the cross product vector \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} = \\sqrt{300} = 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram is \\(\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\\).",
